BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In the Light of the Machine: Toward a Relational Ethics of AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260508T140000
UID:light-machine-toward-relational-ethics-ai@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Moderated by Lisa Deanne Smith\, join our panelists for a time
 ly and thought-provoking conversation on the growing entanglement of AI sy
 stems within our cultural\, economic\, and ecological worlds.\n\nIn the Li
 ght of the Machine: Toward a Relational Ethics of Artificial Intelligence 
 Friday\, May 8\, from 12:00 to 2:00 p.m. Online As AI systems become incre
 asingly entangled with our cultural\, economic\, and ecological worlds\, h
 ow do we negotiate an ethical landscape of emergent intelligence? Moving b
 eyond familiar debates over risk and safety\, this conversation brings tog
 ether panelists who will explore how art can help us sense\, critique\, an
 d reimagine the systems shaping our technological present. By situating AI
  within broader epistemological and cultural contexts. Moderated by Onsite
  Gallery's Senior Curator Lisa Deanne Smith\, this panel seeks to expand A
 I discourse and understand machine learning as a site of relation. In the 
 Light of the Machine: Toward a Relational Ethics of Artificial Intelligenc
 e coincides with Onsite Gallery’s current exhibition Becoming (in the li
 ght of the miracle) guest curated by Farah Yusuf. The panel is live-stream
 ed via YouTube Becoming (in the light of the miracle) is on view at Onsite
  Gallery until May 16\, 2026 Becoming (in the light of the miracle) is gen
 erously supported by the Ontario Arts Council\, an agency of the Governmen
 t of Ontario through the Curatorial Projects: Indigenous and Culturally Di
 verse program.
LOCATION:Online-Only YouTube: https://youtube.com/live/Nu3sLhzo9js?feature
 =share
URL:https://youtube.com/live/Nu3sLhzo9js?feature=share
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
