BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coffee Chat w/ Symon Oliver
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260422T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260422T163000
UID:symon-oliver@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Coffee Chats is a series of casual gatherings with industry gu
 ests. Hosted at the CEAD in small intimate groups\, these gatherings will 
 provide a space for group conversations with practitioners who are interes
 ted in supporting OCAD U students and grads to offer mentorship\, and shar
 e their professional insights and journey\, while collectively creating a 
 community.\n\nCoffee Chat w/ Symon Oliver Date/Time: Wednesday\, April 22\
 , 2026\, 3:30 - 4:30 pm Location: In-person\, CEAD\, 115 McCaul St. 3rd Fl
 oor RSVP to attend Coffee Chats is a series of casual gatherings with indu
 stry guests. Hosted at the CEAD in small intimate groups\, these gathering
 s will provide a space for group conversations with practitioners who are 
 interested in supporting OCAD U students and grads to offer mentorship\, a
 nd share their professional insights and journey\, while collectively crea
 ting a community. Symon Oliver - Founder & Design Director at Tennis As fo
 under and Design Director at Tennis\, I lead the design of systems that tr
 ansform complex challenges into user-centred\, scalable solutions. With ov
 er a decade of experience across UX\, product and experiential design\, di
 gital transformation\, and operational strategy\, I shape intuitive\, resi
 lient experiences that align with user needs and business goals. Studying 
 Design and Media Studies at OCAD University laid the foundation for an app
 roach grounded in research and systems thinking. Early roles in digital re
 search labs led to work in human-centred design\, data visualization\, and
  service innovation—experiences that deepened a commitment to aligning t
 echnology with human needs. At Tennis\, that foundation has evolved into a
  methodology combining holistic design with strategic business goals. We f
 ocus on delivering measurable outcomes—from improving user engagement to
  streamlining operations and enabling organizational change. Instagram Ins
 tagram (Tennis) Website (Tennis) General themes for the talk: Importance o
 f personal brand and marketing Networking Avoid hourly billing (value base
 d pricing) Financial and business literacy **This event will take place at
  the RBC Centre for Emerging Artists & Designers (115 McCaul St\, Level 3)
 . This event will not be recorded to preserve the conversational nature of
  the series. 115 McCaul St is located at the corner of Dundas St and McCau
 l St on the southeast side. All levels of the building can be accessed via
  elevator or stairs. The building is wheelchair accessible. There are gend
 ered washrooms on level 3 and gender-neutral private washrooms on levels 1
  & 2. Spots limited. RSVP Required If you are no longer able to attend\, p
 lease change your RSVP status for us to open the event to others.
LOCATION:Rosalie Sharp Pavillion (MCD) 115 McCaul St. Level 3
URL:https://forms.cloud.microsoft/r/E3Q3xG5J9s
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marketing for Creative Entrepreneurs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260422T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260422T150000
UID:marketing-creative-entrepreneurs@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to stand out without selling out. This workshop cove
 rs branding\, storytelling\, and content strategies to help creative entre
 preneurs attract the right audience and communicate their value clearly. L
 eave with practical ideas for promoting your work in a way that feels alig
 ned with your creative vision.\n\nMarketing for Creative Entrepreneurs. St
 and out without selling out. How to use content and storytelling to grow y
 our business in 2026. Date/Time: Wednesday\, April 22\, 2026\, 1:00 - 3:00
  pm Location (*updated): Online via Zoom. A link to join the webinar will 
 be sent via email closer to the event date to all who RSVP. RSVP to attend
  About Daniel Francavilla : Daniel is a marketer\, educator and founder ob
 sessed with community\, brand and impact. He is a Certified Brand Strategi
 st\, a professor at OCAD University\, a member of the Canadian Marketing A
 ssociation and RGD\, and recipient of a 40 Under 40 Award. Daniel works wi
 th founders and leaders on aligned branding and content through Daniel Doe
 s and Clarity Content. As an advocate for social good\, Daniel founded The
  Good Growth Company to provide training for social good organizations to 
 upskill their teams and scale their mission. He continues to support ACCES
 S\, a nonprofit he founded as a student in 2006\, which provides funding a
 nd mentorship for youth-led initiatives. Previously\, Daniel was an agency
  owner\, founding Now Creative Group in 2013\, which was acquired by King 
 Street Media in 2021\, where he was a partner. About this workshop: Stand 
 out without selling out. Whether you’re offering design services\, jewel
 ry\, illustration\, or another creative product\, marketing is essential t
 o growing your business. This workshop explores how creative entrepreneurs
  can use branding\, storytelling\, and content to attract attention\, conn
 ect with the right audiences\, and communicate value with clarity and inte
 ntion. You’ll leave with practical\, aligned strategies for promoting yo
 ur creative practice\, without feeling inauthentic or overwhelmed. Access 
 Notes: This event is open to OCAD U students and alumni Do not hesitate to
  reach out if you have questions about specific accessibility needs. Pleas
 e email Andrea Rodriguez at entrepreneurship@ocadu.ca
LOCATION:Online-Only
URL:https://forms.office.com/r/Zw64FVfbBP
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GradEx 2026 Plinth Sign-out
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260421T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260513T235959
UID:gradex-2026-plinth-sign-out@ocadu.ca
DESCRIPTION:Plinth Protocol for GradEx 2026\n\nMCA 225A is located at the 
 back of the Ada Slaight Gallery (highlighted in pink on map). Plinths can 
 only be booked in person and during limited times . Visit MCA 225A during 
 the following reservation periods (dates/times may be subject to change so
  check this page 2 days prior to arriving): Tuesday April 21 : 1:00 - 1:30
  pm Tuesday April 28 : 1:00 - 1:30 pm Monday May 4 : 1:00 - 1:30 pm A maxi
 mum of 2 plinths per student can be booked during each reservation period.
  If you require more than 2 plinths\, return the following week and upon a
 vailability you may book 2 more at a time. Plinths can be picked up during
  any of the reservation times listed above\, but you must pick it up by Ma
 y 4\, 1:30pm or your reservation is considered abandoned and it may be giv
 en to someone else. All plinths must be returned to the Ada Slaight Galler
 y no later than May 13 . You may leave them there at any time after GradEx
  with your information taped to the plinth(s). No email requests will be g
 ranted\, must be booked in person. OCAD U ID card is required. If student 
 cannot book in person another student or Faculty may reserve plinths on th
 eir behalf\, but it will be under their name. You must provide the room nu
 mber you will be exhibiting in. Plinths must be returned in the condition 
 you received them in or better. A fee of $150 will be charged for each unr
 eturned or severely damaged plinth.
LOCATION:Ada Slaight Student Gallery 100 McCaul St. 2nd floor
URL:https://www.ocadu.ca/events-and-exhibitions/gradex-2026-plinth-sign-ou
 t
X-SOURCE:OCAD University
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
